      "content": "To appeal to moderates, avoid the word \"collapse\" and instead frame the transition as an economic impossibility that demands excessive government spending. Highlight that without the disciplined fiscal restraint of capitalism, funding universal services while maintaining a growing population inevitably leads to high inflation and lost jobs. Present this not as ideological containment, but as a demographic reality where insufficient economic growth makes large-scale democratic socialism ultimately unsustainable. This shifts the debate from moral preference to practical necessity.",
